WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.601
Meet Keaton Nygren

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.436
He's a law student from Johnstown

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:05.538
who previously interned for Senator

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:08.141
Joni Ernst. Kate Berger.

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.242
Hi, Mr. Vice President.

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:09.776
My question

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:10.877
is, are you prepared

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.145
to push back against the former

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:13.380
president on allegations

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.180
you could have overturned

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.383
the 2020 election?

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:17.183
Okay.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:17.684
Now,

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:21.488
I would refer you to my speech today.

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:24.791
To that question, and the answer is yes.

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:27.660
I think it's it's important.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.262
And not that I didn't

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.830
think there were irregularities

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.233
in the 20, 20 election. I did.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:35.235
And I said so on that fateful day,

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:38.238
I had concerns that there were half a

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:38.872
dozen states

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:40.006
that had changed the rules

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:41.708
in the name of COVID

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:44.010
and that it undermined public confidence

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:45.512
in our elections.

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:47.614
But once states had certified

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:48.348
those elections,

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:49.682
once the courts would review them,

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:50.450
once the Congress

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.852
had considered any objections, I,

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.021
I knew my duty was clear.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.656
The Constitution states

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:58.792
clearly that the job of the

00:00:58.792 --> 00:00:59.559
vice president

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.928
as President of the Senate is to preside

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.430
over a joint session of Congress

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.497
where the Electoral College

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:06.966
votes are opened and counted,

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:09.569
says they shall be opened and they shall

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:11.438
be counted.

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:12.906
And we did that.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:13.807
And I want the American

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:14.774
people to know that

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.177
I believe with all my heart

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:19.212
that we did our duty, that day.

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:20.647
The Bible says he keeps his oath

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:21.481
even when it hurts.

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.850
And I know something about that.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.351
I know the disappointment of the 20,

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.887
20 election. You remember I,

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.222
I was on the ballot.

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:29.789
Right.

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:31.958
But at the end of the day,

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.159
I think the Republican Party

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.695
has to be the party of the Constitution.

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:37.297
I mean, we've had enough of Democrats

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:38.998
trampling on our constitutional rights.

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:40.100
We've got enough of Democrats

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.102
wanting to pack the court,

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:44.104
do away with the Second Amendment,

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.738
this trample on religious freedom.

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:46.773
So now more than ever,

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:47.607
I think the American people

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:48.174
need to be able to look

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.009
to the Republican Party and say

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:50.977
that will be a party

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:52.579
whose leaders are all men and women

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:53.813
that are dedicated

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.048
to preserving and protecting

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:56.883
and defending the Constitution.

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:57.750
Certain states Sure.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.184
On that,

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:00.653
Donald Trump says he is, quote, inclined

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:01.621
to pardon

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.156
many members of the mob

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:05.191
who attacked the Capitol on January six.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.659
Those people were, of course,

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:09.762
part of the same mob who built gallows

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:12.332
and chanted about wanting to hang you.

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:14.033
Would you consider partying

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.335
and pardoning any of them?

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:16.903
You know,

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:17.904
on the day of

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:21.407
January six, I issued a tweet

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:24.277
demanding that people leave the Capitol

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.112
and end the violence.

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:26.646
And I said, that

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:27.614
those who fail to do that

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:28.448
should be prosecuted

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:30.850
to the fullest extent of the law.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.620
And I continue to believe that today

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.122
we cannot ever allow

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:37.690
what happened on January

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.025
six to happen again

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:41.027
in the heart of our democracy.

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:42.962
And I'll stand by the decisions

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:45.798
and the due process of court in our laws

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:49.702
And I have no interest or no intention

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.137
of pardoning those

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:53.673
that assaulted police officers

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.209
or vandalized our Capitol

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:59.078
They need to be answerable to the law.

00:02:59.212 --> 00:02:59.913
Sir, I want to ask

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.915
about some breaking news tonight.

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:03.449
The Justice Department recently

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:05.552
informed Donald Trump's legal team

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:06.753
that he is a target

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:08.121
of a federal investigation

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:10.323
into possibly mishandling

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:12.392
classified documents.

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:14.594
I should say you were cleared last week

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:16.629
in your own documents case.

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:17.931
What's your reaction to the news

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:19.432
about your former boss?

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:20.934
Well, let me say the handling of

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.168
classified materials

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:26.206
is a very serious matter.

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:28.341
And that was why after the revelations

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:31.411
at the president's residence

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.312
and the revelations

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:33.813
at the former president's residence,

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:36.482
I took it upon myself to

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.152
review our files.

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:39.852
And

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.155
we uncovered

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:43.890
a small number of documents

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.225
that have been inadvertently

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:48.027
transferred to our residence in Indiana.

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:49.762
I immediately

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:52.065
informed the Department of Justice, and

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:54.801
I'm grateful

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.169
after our full cooperation

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:56.936
that they concluded

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.571
that it was an innocent mistake.

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:00.106
Do you see his case is different?

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:01.174
But let me say this.

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:04.544
Look, I

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:05.979
I don't know the facts

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:08.448
of the president's case.

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:11.084
I don't know the facts of the former

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:12.752
president's case.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:14.153
And

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:17.690
but what we've got to have in

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.025
this country is equal treatment

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:20.126
under the law.

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:24.797
And, Dana,

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:25.999
you may not know.

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:27.400
I mean, I was very troubled

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.002
last summer when

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:30.570
when for the first time in history,

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:31.604
there was a search warrant

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:33.339
executed at the home of a former

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:34.574
president of the United States.

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:36.209
Surely, you know, all the years

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:37.710
I served on the Judiciary Committee,

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.878
that's when you and I first met.

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:40.380
There had to be

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.147
dozens of ways

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:42.215
that could have been handled

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:44.317
other than that kind of behavior.

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:44.784
I mean,

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:46.452
when I informed the Department of Justice

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:47.253
that we had classified

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:49.055
materials potentially in our home,

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:49.956
they were at my home,

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:51.591
the FBI was on my front doorstep

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:52.959
the next day.

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:54.127
But what we found out

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:55.161
was that when Joe Biden

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:56.162
apparently alerted

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:58.197
the Department of Justice, 80 days later,

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:00.066
they showed up at his office

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:02.702
that's not equal treatment under the law.

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:04.771
We've got him

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:06.806
for treatment.

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:09.309
But the question is allegation

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:10.143
that investigators

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.477
run into obstruction,

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:14.247
which you clearly did not do, if that is

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:17.283
something that investigators see

00:05:17.283 --> 00:05:18.351
as possible,

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:19.285
even enough

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:20.420
potentially to indict

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.021
the former president.

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:24.290
Do you think that that should go forward?

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:28.561
Well, I would I would hope not.

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:29.462
I really would.

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:30.129
Then

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:31.631
I mean,

00:05:33.533 --> 00:05:34.834
there's several reasons for that.

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.869
Number one is I think that

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:37.904
I think it would be terribly

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:39.906
divisive to the country.

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:40.606
I mean, at a time

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:42.041
when the American people are hurting,

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:42.642
I mean, to tell

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:45.078
your families are struggling right now

00:05:45.078 --> 00:05:46.679
with record inflation, we have

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:48.181
we have a crisis at our border,

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:49.515
the likes of which we've never seen.

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:51.217
We have a flood of fentanyl

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:52.385
coming into every city

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:53.720
large and small in this country

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:56.689
that is killing young people every day.

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:58.658
We have threats abroad,

00:05:58.658 --> 00:06:00.026
a crime wave in our cities.

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:01.728
I think now more than ever,

00:06:01.728 --> 00:06:02.729
we ought to be finding ways

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:04.163
we could actually come together.

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:04.731
We're going to get

00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:05.131
this kind

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:06.065
of this kind of action

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:07.233
by the Department of Justice, I

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:08.701
think would only fuel

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:11.170
further division in the country.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:13.005
And let me also say

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:14.173
I think it would also send

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:16.342
a terrible message to the wider world.

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:19.412
I mean, we are the

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:20.913
we're the emblem of democracy.

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:22.281
We're the symbol of justice.

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:22.982
In the world.

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.450
And the

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.718
serious matter,

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:26.552
which has already happened

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:28.221
once in New York

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:29.789
of indicting a former president

00:06:29.789 --> 00:06:30.690
of the United States, sends

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:32.425
a terrible message to the world.

00:06:32.425 --> 00:06:35.194
I hope the DOJ thinks better of it

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:36.429
to resolve these issues

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:37.230
without on a dime.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:38.431
Sir, I just want to clarify

00:06:38.431 --> 00:06:39.065
what you're saying

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:40.266
is that if they believe

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:41.701
he committed a crime,

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:43.703
they should not go forward

00:06:43.703 --> 00:06:45.438
with an indictment.

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:46.205
You just talked before

00:06:46.205 --> 00:06:48.207
about committing to the rule of law.

00:06:48.207 --> 00:06:49.041
Let me be clear that no

00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:50.576
one's above the law. Okay.

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:53.212
But with regard

00:06:53.212 --> 00:06:55.681
to the unique circumstances here,

00:06:57.483 --> 00:06:58.918
look, I

00:06:59.786 --> 00:07:01.320
those classified I had no business

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:02.588
having classified documents

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:04.323
in my residence,

00:07:04.357 --> 00:07:06.392
and I took full responsibility for it.

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:07.126
President Biden

00:07:07.126 --> 00:07:07.860
had no business

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:08.928
having him in his residence

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:11.631
from when he was vice president as well.

00:07:11.631 --> 00:07:13.833
And the same with former President Trump.

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:16.436
But I would just hope

00:07:16.436 --> 00:07:18.771
that there would be a way

00:07:18.771 --> 00:07:19.872
for them to move forward

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:21.841
without the dramatic and drastic

00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:23.342
and divisive step

00:07:23.342 --> 00:07:24.777
of indicting a former president

00:07:24.777 --> 00:07:25.378
of the United States.

00:07:25.378 --> 00:07:26.746
We've got to find a way

00:07:26.746 --> 00:07:28.581
to move our country forward

00:07:28.581 --> 00:07:31.751
and restore confidence in equal treatment

00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:33.186
under the law in this country.

00:07:33.186 --> 00:07:34.620
We really do.

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:38.157
Sir, if Donald Trump

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:40.626
if Donald Trump is convicted of a crime

00:07:41.761 --> 00:07:43.329
and you're elected president,

00:07:43.329 --> 00:07:45.064
would you pardon him?

00:07:45.064 --> 00:07:46.466
Well, I don't want to speak

00:07:46.466 --> 00:07:47.500
about hypotheticals

00:07:49.769 --> 00:07:51.637
I'm not sure I'm going to be elected

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:54.640
president of the United States.

00:07:55.808 --> 00:07:57.910
But I believe we have a fighting chance.

00:07:57.944 --> 00:07:59.245
I really believe we do.

00:07:59.245 --> 00:08:00.179
And if you are

00:08:00.179 --> 00:08:01.948
and I would hope again,

00:08:01.948 --> 00:08:04.851
then you're as persistent

00:08:04.851 --> 00:08:05.818
as ever

00:08:07.887 --> 00:08:10.056
CNN is living up to its reputation.

00:08:11.057 --> 00:08:12.225
But look, there are real issues

00:08:12.225 --> 00:08:13.493
the American people are facing.

00:08:13.493 --> 00:08:15.361
And rather than talking about that,

00:08:15.361 --> 00:08:16.562
I want to talk about with the people

00:08:16.562 --> 00:08:17.330
here in Iowa,

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.030
talking about

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.532
which is the failed policies

00:08:19.532 --> 00:08:21.434
of the Biden administration,

00:08:21.701 --> 00:08:23.536
the need for us to have new leadership

00:08:23.536 --> 00:08:25.571
in the White House and in our party.

00:08:25.638 --> 00:08:25.938
We have.

